{"ts": "2026-10-28T22:35:37.513641Z", "run_id": "r-20261028T2235Z-216c", "unit": "openspec:add-oidc-login", "seq": 7, "type": "task.started", "task": "6.1", "title": "6.1 Write `src/identity/oidc/login.test.ts` first (`buildServer` from `src/api` with `sequentialIds()`, `noopTracer` and a silent logger; `startFakeOidc`; scenarios \"Authorization request\", \"Provider down at login\", \"No issuer\" (routes half; it first asserts `typeof registerOidcRoutes === \"function\"`, then calls `GET /health`) and \"A half-wired engine is refused\" (`registerOidcRoutes` half)), then implement `registerOidcRoutes` in `src/identity/oidc/routes.ts` (a null `config` registers the three routes answering 503 `{ error: { code: \"OIDC_NOT_CONFIGURED\", message: \"Sign-in is not configured\" } }`; a `config` without `pool` or `engineKey` throws `OidcError` `OIDC_NOT_CONFIGURED`; otherwise it builds the client with `createOidcClient` and registers the login route; the callback and logout routes are added by tasks 6.2 and 6.4), the login handler in `src/identity/oidc/login.ts` as in design.md decision 5 (`cache-control: no-store`), and `createSealer` in `src/identity/oidc/seal.ts`: key = `hkdfSync(\"sha256\", utf8(key.reveal()), \"\", info, 32)` (text under 32 characters: `OIDC_SEAL_INVALID`), AES-256-GCM with a fresh 12-byte IV and `aad = info + \"\\n\" + extra`, output `base64url(iv + ciphertext + tag)`, `open` returning `null` for anything malformed, altered or sealed under another key or aad; the login cookie uses info `ursitoare/login`, implementing requirements \"Login starts an authorization-code flow with PKCE\" and \"OIDC is optional and configured by three variables\""}
